Commentary of al-Sam'ani (Tafsir al-Quran) on surah 5, verse 52:

The words of Allah, the Exalted: ﴿So you see those in whose hearts is a disease﴾ meaning: hypocrisy (nifaq). ﴿They hasten toward them﴾ meaning: toward supporting them and allying with them. There is an ellipsis (hadhf) in this, as Allah, the Exalted, said: ﴿And ask the town﴾, meaning: the people of the town. ﴿They say, "We fear lest a misfortune should befall us"﴾. Ibn 'Abbas said: its meaning is, "We fear that the affair of Muhammad will not be completed, so the matter will turn against us." Others said: its meaning is, "We fear that there will be a drought, so they will not show us favor with fruits," since the Jews were the owners of the palm trees and fruits. The first interpretation is more sound.

﴿Perhaps Allah will bring a conquest or a decision from Him﴾. It was said: He meant by this the conquest of Makkah. It was also said: it is the conquest of the Jewish settlements, such as Khaybar, Fadak, Tayma' and Wadi al-Qura. ﴿Or a decision from Him﴾. It was said: it is the completion of Muhammad's affair. It was said: it is the expulsion of the Banu al-Nadir. It was said: it is the killing of the Banu Qurayzah. It was said: it is the informing of the names of the hypocrites, so that they would be disgraced. {So they will become, over what they had concealed within themselves, regretful}
